From c9e40d006ed4731544a04735e5d057193989725a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 18:06:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 482/572] fix: use #ifdef for __aarch64__ flags

The __aarch64__ is only defined, without a value, it shoudl be checked
with #ifdef.
This corrects -Wundef GCC warning.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 0d9813616bf114471f76abc93e1b7f18727c3bc3 fix: use #ifdef for __aarch64__ flags]
